reer Pathways Podcast Related Explore Lyon Career Pathways Podcast We can't wait to meet you Schedule a visit Apply Today Welcome to the Career Pathways Podcast page! Lyon College is proud to announce the launch of its engaging and informative podcast, \"Career Pathways,\" providing valuable insights into the world of careers, college life, and more. Hosted by Lyon College’s Director of Career Services, Patrick Lynch, and co-hosted by Lyon students Gavin Brunson and Jayson Nichols, this podcast promises to be a valuable resource for a wide range of listeners. The \"Career Pathways\" podcast caters to a diverse audience, making it a must-listen for: College Students: Both current students and those considering higher education will find valuable guidance to help shape their career paths. Early Career Professionals: In today's ever-evolving world of work, young professionals seeking to navigate the early stages of their careers will discover invaluable advice and insights. Parents: Parents of college students and early career professionals can gain a better understanding of the challenges and opportunities their children face. Curious Minds: Anyone interested in diverse topics, from marketing, technology, and tennis to pop culture and the timeless works of art created by Will Ferrell, will find something intriguing in this podcast. Be sure to check out the episodes below to get started on your pathway to career success! Introduction to Career Pathways Career Pathways is an educational show designed to help you and others find the perfect career. Our show brings on guests who are professors and or experienced in a field to tell you about Careers and what paths you could go down or create. Join Pat Lynch, Gavin Brunson, and Jayson Nichols as they walk you through the world of College and the careers you can choose. Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Episode 1: Are There Jobs for an Archaeologist? The question that is asked all the time when coming into a field like Anthropology or Archeology is the question of jobs, can you even get a job with a degree in these? Today Patrick Lynch will find the answer to that question, by dissecting the mind of Dr. Jason Kennedy, Assistant Professor of Anthropology. Join Pat and his two co-host Gavin and Jayson on their first episode of Career Pathways, as they go through the mind and life of Jason Kennedy and get the answers you want to know. Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Episode 2: Anthropology, What the Heck is it? In todays episode, Pat Lynch sits down with Dr. Matthew Lebrato, Assistant Director of Anthropology. He will dissect anthropology and what it means to be an Anthropologist. Join Pat, Gavin and Jayson, as they pick the brain of Dr. Lebrato and find out what type of careers and jobs you can get with an Anthropology major! Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Episode 3: If I Could Talk to the Animals (Psychology Majors) In this episode of The Career Pathways Podcast, Pat and Jayson discuss with Dr. Florkiewicz the evolution from monkeys to humans and discuss the jobs and careers you can achieve with a Psychology major. Join Pat and Jayson as they pick the brain of Dr. Florkiewicz about a multitude of things! Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Episode 4: So You Wanna Be a Rock 'N' Roll Star? (Music Careers) Have you ever wanted to be a rock 'n' roll star? Or maybe you just want to make music? Well Career Pathways might just help you with that on today's episode. Pat Lynch and Jayson Nichols interview and learn from veteran musician Jack Wells on life in acting to life as a musician and what career options there are in the field. Join Pat Lynch and Jayson Nichols, as they learn the ins and outs of what it takes to be a rock n' roll star! Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Episode 5: Journey to the Center of the Mind (Social Psychology) Have you ever wondered why some people are more proned to being extroverts than others? Or why and how parasocial relationships work? Or maybe you are looking for a career in Psychology and don't know where to start! Well then you will love this weeks episode with Social Psychology Professor Dr. Jennifer Daniels! Pat, Jayson and Gavin, will learn and explore the deeps of the mind and what makes us human! Join us as we host Dr. Jennifer Daniels on this weeks episode! Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Episode 6:  Starting Your Own Business, Entrepreneurship (Featuring Mike Clauss) Have you ever thought about starting your own business? Or maybe you want to start and run a company in the future! Well on this morning's episode Pat Lynch will sit down with entrepreneur Mike Clauss to talk about starting business and rebranding failure. Join us this morning as we pick the brain of Mike Clauss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts [SPECIAL] Thanksgiving Special - Career Pathways On this episode of the Career Pathways podcast, the crew talks about what they are thankful for and what they have learned over the past four months. Join Pat, Gavin and Jayson on this week's special episode. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 7: Biology Puns so Funny They \"Cell\" Themselves - Cell Biology (Featuring Dr. Alexander Beeser) On this mornings episode of The Career Pathways podcast, Pat Lynch and Jayson Nichols sit down with Cell Biologist and Professor of Biology Dr. Alexander \"Sandy\" Beeser. He explains what it takes to get into medical school and what you need to become a biologist. Join us this morning as we pick the brain of Dr. Beeser! Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts [SPECIAL] Winter Break, Final EP of The Year!! - Career Pathways On this episode of the Career Pathways podcast, Patrick and Jayson send off the year with a simple short special episode to thank everyone and wrap up the year as a whole, Enjoy and have a great holiday! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 8: How do Politicians Party? They Caucus! Politics and Careers (Featuring Skip Rutherford) As Bill Clinton once said: \"Being president is like running a cemetery: you've got a lot of people under you and nobody's listening.\" And on this mornings episode of The Career Pathways podcast, Pat Lynch and Jayson Nichols sit down with Skip Rutherford, the first dean of the Clinton School of Public Service and an advisor on the Clinton Campaign. Skip will talk about his experience with the campaign and his experience with the politics, well also giving key insights to the world we live in. Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Youtube Episode 9: People Were Really Mad Over That Being On TV??? Careers in TV & News (Featuring Victoria Capek) That TV host is nuts, but her show is a-peeling! Have you ever thought about going into Television and or TV production? Well on this mornings episode of The Career Pathways podcast, Pat Lynch, Gavin Brunson and Jayson Nichols sit down with Victoria Capek, a TV journalist and the host of Good Morning Arkansas. Victoria will talk about her time in the News industry and talk about all the pros and cons of working in the industry at such a young age. She will also talk her career on TikTok and how that affected her time in the News industry. This episode is easily one of our best so far, so stay tuned till the end. Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Youtube Episode 10: Tattoos and Literature? Careers in Literature and Languages (Featuring. Dr. James Martell) What’s the difference between cats and a comma? Cats have claws at the end of their paws and commas are a pause at the end of a clause. In today's episode, Pat, Gavin and Jayson sit down with Dr. James Martell a professor of romance languages and Literary studies. Dr. Martell will explain the in's and outs of the journey to his profession and will also explain the amazing sleeve of tattoos that he has. This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Youtube Episode 11: Data Science & Social Media? Careers in Data Science (Featuring Marcus Birkenkrahe) On today's episode of The Career Pathways Podcast, Patrick, Gavin and Jayson sit down with Dr. Marcus Birkenkrahe. Dr Marcus Birkenkrahe is a German physicist, a founder of the internet, and a Professor of Computer & Data science at Lyon College. Dr. Birkenkrahe will discuss everything from Data Science, to the start of the internet, and also to touchy subjects like AI. Spotify Apple Podcasts Google Podcasts Youtube Episode 12: Wait What Is Trying To Get Passed In Congress? Poli-Sci Careers (Featuring Dr. Brendan Connell) The opposite of “pro” is “con,” so the opposite of progress is … Congress. On today's episode of The Career Pathways Podcast, Patrick, Gavin and Jayson sit down with Dr. Brendan Connell to talk about immigration and United States' foreign policy. Dr. Connell will explain everything from political divide to Ultra-Marathoning? Join us as we dive into the amazing mind of Brendan Connell. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 13: Are Video Games Really A Sport? Esports (Featuring Luke Johnson) Why did the computer keep freezing at the gaming tournament? It was just too cool for school. On today's episode of the Carrer Pathways Podcast, Pat and Producer Jayson interview Luke Johnson, the director of Esports at Lyon College with special host Noah Theis. Luke will explain what it takes to become an Esports player and why people should join Esports. He also will talk about a fan-con hosted in the Batesville area. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube [SPECIAL] Sit Down With Abigail Smithson, Host of Dear Adam Silver. On this episode of the Career Pathways podcast, Patrick, Gavin, Radek and Jayson sit down with Abigail Smithson, a former professor of art at Lyon College and current host of the podcast Dear Adam Silver. Abigail will talk about everything from California to the NBA. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 14: What Jobs Are There For Communication Majors?? (Featuring Dr. Kim Kulovitz) I asked the audience if anyone had experience with public speaking. A cricket in the corner started chirping. Today, Patrick takes a backseat as MK, Sydney and Gavin sit down with Dr. Kim Kulovitz, the assistant professor of Communication. They will talk about a wide arrange of topics, from jobs for Communication Majors to the use of AI in the classroom. This is one you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 15: Getting Active in College and The Community! (Featuring Dr. Brandii Peterson) The Trio? I know that! That's the song that plays at the end of The Good The Bad, And The Ugly! In today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast. Dr. Brandii Peterson, Executive Director of TRiO at Lyon College. In the episode Pat and Gavin will sit down with her and discuss a wide range of topics from her work with the Tyler Perry company, to the TRiO program, and to Goodwill?? This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 16: Is The U.S. Economy Stable??? Economics (Featuring Dr. Radek Szulga) In today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast,.Dr. Radek Szulga (Professor of Economics) will tell us whether one-handed Economists really exist. In the episode Pat and Radek will sit down and discuss a wide range of topics from the U.S. economy to the world economy and what's really going on currently. This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 17: English And The State of Liberal Arts Education - English (Featuring Dr. Wesley Beal) Well clearly this guy doesn't need to use Grammarly! In today's episode of the Career Pathways Podcast, Dr. Wesley Beal (Professor of English) will sit down with Pat Lynch and will talk about an array of things. From the State of Liberal Arts Education, to the intricate subtopics of the John Dos Passos Society, Dr. Beal will will go in-depth and give his two sense on all things English. This is an episode you don't wanna miss. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 18: How Do You Grade Creativity? - Art (Featuring Dr. Dustyn Bork) Art you glad you listened to this Podcast? Today Pat and Gavin will sit down with Dustyn Bork (Professor of Art) and will discuss a wide array of things, from creativity and how you grade it, to the things people do and do not get right about art and art majors. This is an episode you don't wanna miss. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 19: Should You Do International Studies!? - International Education (Featuring Nicolas Pattillo) Austin Powers is not the only international man of mystery. Today Pat will sit down with Nicolas Pattillo (Director of International Education) and will discuss a wide array of topics, from international education post-Covid, to traveling to so many countries he can't even count all of them. This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube [SPECIAL] All Things Huckleberry! (Featuring MK, Sydney, Pat and Jayson) In today's episode of the Career Pathways Podcast, Pat, MK, Sydney and Jayson will sit down and try all things huckleberry, while Pat berates them with huckleberry questions and facts. This is an episode you don't wanna miss. Youtube Music Youtube [SPECIAL] All Things Poland (Featuring JM & Dr. Szulga) A Polish man, a Hillbilly and basically a Canadian walk into a podcast studio, who is walking out? The long awaited Poland recap is here! In today's episode of the podcast, Jayson brings on John Michael and Radek Szulga. They will discuss all their crazy and wacky adventures on the funniest episode of the Career Pathways podcast ever. This is absolutely one you don't wanna miss. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 20: What Does It Take to Coach? - Coaching (Featuring Chris Douglas) In today's episode of the Career Pathways Podcast, Pat sits down with Lyon College's Football coach Chris Douglas to discuss coaching. What does it take to coach and how do you manage a team of a 100+ members? This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 21: A Lesson In Leadership - Faculty (Featuring President Melissa Taverner) The State of The Union? Oh wrong president. In today's episode of the Career Pathways Podcast, Pat and Gavin sit down with the president of Lyon College, Dr. Melissa Taverner. She will explain everything from what it takes to be a leader, to why Liberal Arts still matters. This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 22: Creative Writing and Book Bans? (Featuring Garrard Conley) In today's episode of the Career Pathways Podcast, Jayson and Pat sit down with Garrard Conley, Professor of Creative Writing and published author. Conley will talk about all things from his memoir to how to write creatively. This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Student Entrepreneurs: Varsity Vintage and Clothing (Featuring Drew Chalberg) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast. Gavin sits down and hosts Drew Chalberg, Student entrepreneur at Lyon College. Drew runs Varsity Vintage, a vintage clothing and record store. This is an episode you don't wanna miss. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 23: Biology and... Evolved Humans?? Biology (Featuring Dr. Cassia Oliveira) Are Biologists sales people? Because we heard they sell themselves! In today's episode of the Career Pathways Podcast, Pat sits down Dr. Cassia Oliveira, Professor of Biology at Lyon College. Pat and her will discuss everything from the evolution of humans to- potatoes? This is an episode you don't want to miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube [Special] International Student Association. On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast. Patrick sits down with three graduating students who are apart of ISA, Lyon College's International Student Association. This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube [Special] The Send Off. Today, Pat, Gavin and Jayson sit down and reflect on the year as a whole. This is an episode you don't want to miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 24: Did George Washington Have Wooden Teeth? - History (Featuring Dr. Kieran O'Keefe) Blasting to the past with this episode. On today's episode, Pat will sit down with Kieran O'Keefe, Professor of History. They will discuss everything from George Washington's teeth to the most accurate movies of the Revolutionary War. This is an episode you don't wanna miss. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 25: The Diversity of Cities and India with Dr. Scott Roulier. Cities and... Philosophy!? How does that work? Well today Pat Lynch sits down with Dr. Scott Roulier, the professor of Political Philosophy to talk about a large assortment of things, from population growth, why some places are the way they are and the politics of India? Watch the episode to find out more! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 26: Why Insects and Bugs Matter! - (Ft. Dr. Eric South, Professor of Entomology) Stoneflies, Music? And the world of Entomology is the spotlight of today's episode! Sit down with Pat and Gavin as they interview Lyon College's Dr. Eric South on the world of Entomology and why it matters to our world! Note: Dr. South would like to say that the comment made about \"red tide\" algal bloom is incorrect and that he misspoke when talking about it. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 27: How do Religion and Philosophy work together? (Ft. Dr. Paul Bube) Buddha or Aristotle? Why not both! In this episode of the Career Pathways Podcast, Dr. Paul Bube will go in depth on religion and philosophy and how the two can coexist and connect to each other. Join Pat Lynch and Gavin Brunson as they explore the world's of these two mediums! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 27: We are Teaching Math Wrong!? (Featuring Dr. Wesley Perkins) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast, Pat Lynch and Gavin Brunson sit down with Dr. Wesley Perkins (Professor of Mathematics) to talk about all things mathematics. From careers to teaching methods, Dr. Perkins will dive into the world of math to help us simpletons understand it! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 28: A Living Legend Teaches Us English (Featuring Dr. Terrell Tebbetts) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast producer Jayson gets an exclusive sit-down interview with Dr. Terrell Tebbetts. Dr. Tebbetts is a living legend amongst Lyon College and has been a key figure in the English department for over fifty years! Dr. Tebbetts will talk about everything from the importance of English, to his deep connection with poetry, and to the history of Lyon itself. Join us on a special episode, as Pat steps aside to let two children of the humanities have a great conversation. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 29: Class Is In Session! Education Majors (Featuring Dr. Kim Crosby and Dr. Maggie Campbell Webb) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast Pat sits down with Dr. Maggie Campbell and Dr. Kim Crosby to talk about education majors and Lyon College's new Education masters program. This is an episode you don't want to miss. Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 30: Booze and Bones? Anthropology (featuring Dr. Jason Kennedy) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast Pat and Jayson sit down with returning guest Dr. Jason Kennedy to talk about human bones. Dr. Kennedy will explain how we can tell gender and age from these bones and how it ties into Booze!?? This is an episode you don't want to miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 31: How To Overcome Freshman Year - First Year Advising (Ft. John [JM] Michael Stastny) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast Gavin and Producer Jayson sit down with Lyon's newest and youngest staff member John (JM) Michael Stastny. JM is a first year advisor at Lyon college and talks a lot about new students and how to make it through the first year hump. At the end of this episode there are also bloopers from a camera issue. This is an episode you don't want to miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 32: Becoming A Leader On and Off The Court (Ft. Coach Rodney Mayes) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast, Gavin and guest host Luke Bridges sit down with Lyon's men's basketball coach Rodney Mayes. Coach Mayes will talk about everything from leadership to using your skills on and off the court. This is an episode you don't want to miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Special Episode: All Things Possible: The Solution - Love Across The Network. (Ft. Timothy & Lavonica Davis) All Things Possible: The Solution, with Barretta Robinson is a podcast that spotlights people through all walks of life, succeeding through their hard work with the help of the lord. The podcast is part of a mini series hosted by Career Pathways that is intertwined bi-weekly with other mini series and podcasts on every Friday. This week's episode has Barretta sitting down with Timothy and Lavonica Davis, authors of the book \"A Message Notification\". Tim and Lavonica will explain their background, their story, and how their faith kept them strong even through the vast social network of Facebook. This is an episode of All Things Possible you don't want to miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Special Episode: Election Overview (Ft. Dr. Jaeyun Sung & Dr. Brendan Connell) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast, Pat and Producer Jayson sit down with Dr. Jaeyun Sung and Dr. Brendan Connell, both professors of political science. They will go over the 2024 Presidential election, with its misconceptions, truths, and voting patterns. They will explain it all! This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Episode 33: What Does It Mean To Work In The Chamber?? (Ft. Crystal Johnson) On today's episode of the Career Pathways podcast, Pat and Producer Jayson sit down with Crystal Johnson, the CEO of the Batesville Chamber of Commerce. She will explain everything from what it's like to be the CEO of a chamber, to the wacky things that happen in a small town. This is an episode you don't wanna miss! Spotify Apple Podcasts Youtube Music Youtube Lyon College Start Your Future Lyon is more than just a college. It's a community distinguished by its academic curriculum, unique honor and social systems, and award-winning professors. Apply Today Contact Resources Contact Us Event Request Application Give Job Opportunities Marketing Request News Report a Concern Footer Right Nav Course & Exam Schedules Stay Connected Style Guide Net Price Calculator The Highlander Newspaper Community Calendar tik-tok-icon-black 2300 Highland Road • Batesville, Arkansas 72501 • Phone: (870) 307-7000 • Fax: (870) 307-7001 2026 © Speak Creative. All rights reserved. Sitemap | Privacy Policy |"
